ZJU Research OS (zju-research-skills)
Copyright 2026 ZJU Research Skills Project

This plugin contains original distilled workflows and a Research Mission
orchestration protocol released under Apache-2.0.
It was designed with reference to the following open projects. No upstream
repository is vendored wholesale. See provenance/sources.yaml for exact pinned
commits, files consulted, licenses, and the scope of adaptation.

- Yuan1z0825/nature-skills, Apache-2.0. Nature-style Chinese research workflow
  patterns for search, access, writing, monitoring, figures, presentations,
  review, data availability, proposals, patents, and integrity boundaries.
- K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills, MIT. Reproducible literature-search,
  statistical-analysis, scientific-writing, testing, and safety patterns.
- jaechang-hits/SciAgent-Skills, CC BY 4.0. Life-science evaluation ideas and
  biostatistical task coverage.
- yorkeccak/scientific-skills, MIT. Natural-language source-routing ideas for
  literature, biomedical, and chemistry discovery.
- agentskills/agentskills, Apache-2.0. Agent Skills open-format conventions.
- sickn33/agentic-awesome-skills, MIT. Portfolio selection, evidence-manifest,
  and deterministic validation concepts.
- wanshuiyin/Auto-claude-code-research-in-sleep, MIT. Untrusted-content,
  provenance, experiment-handoff, and review-gate concepts.
- Galaxy-Dawn/claude-scholar, MIT. Skill-quality scorecard and remediation
  concepts.
- WUBING2023/PaperSpine, MIT. Contribution-first, results-validation, and
  reviewer-readiness gate concepts.

Imbad0202/academic-research-skills (CC BY-NC 4.0) and
HKUSTDial/Supervisor-Skills (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) were inspected only to compare
capability coverage. No protected text, templates, or workflow expression from
those repositories is incorporated into this Apache-2.0 distribution.

